Package: com.huhansibuxin.searchpartyquiet
Name: SearchPartyQuiet
Version: 1.0.5
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Description: Kills the 50-93% one-to-ten-second CPU spikes of searchpartyd by rebinding, inside that one daemon, the arm64e auth-GOT slot of _sqlite3_step and returning SQLITE_DONE for INSERT/REPLACE into observation tables (ObservedAdvertisement / observations / BeaconObservation / LocationProvider). With Find My Network disabled (UserOptOut) these observation writes are pure background garbage that bloat Observations.db to 263MB / 91% dead pages and trigger 4MB WAL checkpoint storms every 15 minutes. DELETE / UPDATE / PRAGMA / SELECT always pass through, so the built-in prune + incremental_vacuum keep reclaiming dead pages. No plist or database file is ever written; no Foundation/UIKit/Logos/substrate/ellekit link; a single PAC-signed slot is swapped with numeric discriminator verification and fail-open on any uncertainty. A 4-starts-per-5-minutes breaker downgrades to stock SQLite to prevent the 11-14 style crash loop. v1.0.5 CLEAN: all on-disk logging compiled out - the tweak never opens/writes any log file (hook, PAC rebind and crash breaker are byte-for-byte identical to v1.0.4). Flags still supported in /var/mobile/Documents/SearchPartyQuiet/ (or /var/tmp): PASSTHROUGH_ALL (stock), DISABLED (no hooks); touch then kickstart -k user/501/com.apple.icloud.searchpartyd.
Maintainer: huhansibuxin
Author: huhansibuxin
Section: Tweaks
Depends: ellekit
